  "llm_summary": "The latest GDELT feed highlights a surge in climate‑related security incidents: Egypt’s severe flooding, Indonesia’s focus on food and water resilience, and a cascade of El Niño impacts that the UN warns could push ≈ 49 million people into acute hunger. In Latin America, worsening El Niño conditions are forecast to deepen food insecurity, while a southern Honduras municipality has declared a drought emergency affecting over 15,000 families. Together, these events illustrate a widening geographic footprint of climate‑driven resource stress, straining food and water systems and increasing the likelihood of humanitarian and political instability. The exchange‑rates source, though not detailed here, likely reflects the economic pressures these crises impose on vulnerable economies."
